editor_description = "Medium (ADR 18: 1.0 m cube, one storage cell). Inherited from crate.tscn rather than duplicated, so crate.gd's dozen exported tuning values (hold_stiffness, drag_reach, shove_force, settle_frames...) stay in sync across all three sizes automatically -- the first time they drifted by hand, a Medium would feel different from a Small for no reason anyone could find. Inheritance also means the SceneReplicationConfig is authored once. Root mass below is only the pre-setup() fallback; Crate.setup() overwrites it per-instance from the record's own mass -- a Medium can be light textiles or heavy masonry (ADR 25 (c): weight decides, not size)."
mass = 40.0

